; A `.cbor` payload whose TARGET carries no value of its own — a bare fixed value (`bytes .cbor 42`)
; or one behind any number of mandatory TAGS (`bytes .cbor #6.1(42)`) — in MEMBER / element
; position. Generates under EVERY profile; the rows are the regression carrier for that.
;
; Without encodings a fixed value stores nothing, so the `Fixed` deserialize branch evaluates to the
; unit `()` and emits it through whatever before/after wrapper its caller supplies — including the
; staging expression a `.cbor` overload wraps its target's read in. Where the wrapper binds nothing
; the line is suppressed instead, so a caller that supplies none (which is every caller outside a
; payload) gets the same bytes it always got.
;
; Value-less-ness is a property of the whole encoding CHAIN, so the payload arm's test recurses
; through `Tagged`: a mandatory tag stores nothing of its own without encodings either, its number
; being a constant verified on the way past. Testing the ROOT alone staged the tagged spelling and
; re-emitted the binding as a bare expression line in a discarding statement slot — not Rust, and an
; abort at rustfmt rather than a refusal, while the same spec exited 0 under `--preserve-encodings`.
;
; The class covers every fixed kind (`42`, `"s"`, `true`, `null`), both the bare and the keyed
; element spellings, and stacked tags — it keys on a value-less chain under a `.cbor`, not on the
; constant, the key, or the tag depth:
;   - `x`  the bare untagged element.
;   - `y`  a tag between the `.cbor` and the constant, bare element.
;   - `z`  the same behind an ARRAY member key.
;   - `m`  the same behind a MAP member key — the position that actually aborted under this
;          catalog's flags, since a map entry's presence closure supplies the statement slot the
;          staged binding could not be a bare expression in (the array positions aborted only under
;          `--annotate-fields=false`, which no catalog row can spell).
;   - `s`  stacked tags, which the test has to RECURSE through rather than peek one level.
; One neighbour is deliberately NOT it: the rule-BODY spelling `x = bytes .cbor 42` is refused
; GRACEFULLY one seam earlier, by the bare-fixed-value rule-body rejection, and never reaches the
; deserialize walk.
;
; These rows are generate-only, so they hold the ABORT class alone. That the emitted crate builds
; and round-trips byte-exactly — payload verified, tag verified, payload exhaustion enforced,
; non-minimal payload and tag heads preserved — is pinned by
; `cbor_payload_over_fixed_value_generates_and_round_trips_on_every_profile`.
;
; Surfaced by the recombination sweep (`outer=arr_single inner=cbor_payload filler=type2.value`)
; once the tagged-optional member kind reshuffled its seeded draws onto the composition.
x = [bytes .cbor 42]
y = [bytes .cbor #6.1(42)]
z = [k: bytes .cbor #6.1(42)]
m = { k: bytes .cbor #6.1(42) }
s = [bytes .cbor #6.1(#6.2(42))]
